# Coding Standards (TypeScript)

- **TypeScript strict.** No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no dynamic property-access hacks.
  If you need one, you don't understand the type — read it and model it correctly.
- **Naming:** `camelCase` vars/functions, `PascalCase` types/components/classes,
  `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` constants, kebab-case files (`PascalCase.tsx` for React components).
- **Imports at the top of the file only.** Access other modules via their public barrel;
  never deep-import their internals.
- **Config/secrets:** read env only through a validated config module; never scatter
  `process.env`. Never log or commit secrets/tokens/PII.
- **Errors:** typed, fail loudly, never swallowed.
- **Comments:** default none — rely on good names; comment only non-obvious *why*. Never
  describe the diff.
- **Persistence:** Prisma migrations for all schema changes; never hand-edit generated artifacts.
- **Dependencies:** prefer versions published ≥7 days ago; no floating ranges (`latest`, `*`).
- **Tests:** do not edit tests just to make them pass.

